export const chapter = {"id":"ch21","part":"第 5 部　後段：測試與封裝","partEn":"Part 5: Backend & Packaging","partId":"part-5","num":21,"shortTitle":"先進封裝","shortTitleEn":"Advanced Packaging","fullTitle":"第 21 章　先進封裝：把多顆晶片整合在一起","fullTitleEn":"Chapter 21: Advanced Packaging — Integrating Multiple Chips into One","category":"backend","waferTrack":"- 前一站：晶圓測試，挑出了好的晶粒\r\n- **本章：先進封裝，把多顆晶片整合成一個系統**\r\n- 下一站：最終測試","waferTrackEn":"- Previous stop: wafer test, the good dies have been identified\r\n- **This chapter: advanced packaging, integrating several chips into one system**\r\n- Next stop: final test","headings":[{"text":"為什麼需要先進封裝","id":"為什麼需要先進封裝"},{"text":"2.5D：並排放在中介層上","id":"25d並排放在中介層上"},{"text":"扇出型封裝","id":"扇出型封裝"},{"text":"3D 堆疊：往上疊","id":"3d-堆疊往上疊"},{"text":"小晶片（Chiplet）","id":"小晶片chiplet"},{"text":"先進封裝的挑戰","id":"先進封裝的挑戰"},{"text":"2.5D、扇出型與 3D／3.5D 封裝條例總覽","id":"已知25d扇出型與3d封裝條例總覽"},{"text":"定量物理定律與 3D 製程視窗","id":"定量物理定律與3d製程視窗"},{"text":"現場異常徵兆與跨站根因排查","id":"現場異常徵兆與跨站根因排查"},{"text":"本章重點","id":"本章重點"},{"text":"延伸閱讀","id":"延伸閱讀"}],"headingsEn":[{"text":"Why advanced packaging is needed","id":"why-advanced-packaging-is-needed"},{"text":"2.5D: side by side on an interposer","id":"25d-side-by-side-on-an-interposer"},{"text":"Fan-out packaging","id":"fan-out-packaging"},{"text":"3D stacking: building upward","id":"3d-stacking-building-upward"},{"text":"Chiplets","id":"chiplets"},{"text":"Challenges of advanced packaging","id":"challenges-of-advanced-packaging"},{"text":"2.5D, Fan-Out & 3D/3.5D Packaging Clauses","id":"known-25d-fan-out-and-3d-packaging-clauses"},{"text":"Quantitative Governing Laws & 3D Process Windows","id":"quantitative-governing-laws-and-3d-process-windows"},{"text":"Fab Failure Signatures & Root-Cause Diagnostics","id":"failure-signatures-and-root-cause-diagnostics"},{"text":"Key takeaways","id":"key-takeaways"},{"text":"Further reading","id":"further-reading"}],"contentHtml":"<h1 id=\"第-21-章-先進封裝把多顆晶片整合在一起\" class=\"heading-anchor\">第 21 章　先進封裝：把多顆晶片整合在一起<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#第-21-章-先進封裝把多顆晶片整合在一起\" aria-hidden=\"true\">#</a></h1>\n<div class=\"callout callout-wafer-pos\"><div class=\"callout-badge\">📍 WAFER TRACK 晶圓站點</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p class=\"semi-p\">📍 <strong>晶圓位置</strong></p>\n<ul class=\"semi-ul\"><li>前一站：晶圓測試，挑出了好的晶粒</li><li><strong>本章：先進封裝，把多顆晶片整合成一個系統</strong></li><li>下一站：最終測試</li></ul></div></div>\n<hr class=\"semi-hr\" />\n<h2 id=\"為什麼需要先進封裝\" class=\"heading-anchor\">為什麼需要先進封裝<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#為什麼需要先進封裝\" aria-hidden=\"true\">#</a></h2>\n<p class=\"semi-p\">過去，提升晶片效能主要靠微縮電晶體。但現在這條路越走越難、越走越貴，還遇到幾個限制：</p>\n<ul class=\"semi-ul\"><li><strong>晶粒不能無限大</strong>：一顆晶粒的大小，受限於曝光機一次能曝光的範圍，大約 26 mm × 33 mm。</li><li><strong>大晶粒良率低</strong>：第 16 章提到，晶粒越大，越容易被缺陷打中。</li><li><strong>不同功能適合不同製程</strong>：運算核心適合最先進的製程，類比和輸入輸出電路用成熟製程就夠了，記憶體則需要專門的製程。</li><li><strong>頻寬需求暴增</strong>：人工智慧運算需要在處理器和記憶體之間搬運大量資料。</li></ul>\n<p class=\"semi-p\">於是產業開始把一顆大晶片拆成幾顆小晶片，各自用最適合的製程製造，再用先進封裝把它們緊密地整合在一起，讓它們像一顆晶片一樣運作。封裝不再只是「保護」，而成了提升效能的關鍵。</p>\n<hr class=\"semi-hr\" />\n<h2 id=\"25d並排放在中介層上\" class=\"heading-anchor\">2.5D：並排放在中介層上<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#25d並排放在中介層上\" aria-hidden=\"true\">#</a></h2>\n<p class=\"semi-p\"><strong>2.5D 封裝</strong>把好幾顆晶片並排放在一片<strong>中介層</strong>上。中介層本身通常是一片矽，上面有非常細密的導線，讓晶片之間可以高速、大量地互相溝通；中介層再透過 TSV 連到下方的封裝基板。</p>\n<p class=\"semi-p\">最典型的例子，是把處理器和多組 HBM 記憶體並排放在同一片中介層上。中介層甚至可以透過多次曝光拼接，做得比單次曝光的範圍還大。</p>\n<p class=\"semi-p\"><!-- 圖：2.5D 封裝剖面（處理器與 HBM 並排於中介層上，中介層下方為基板） --></p>\n<div class=\"callout callout-glossary\"><div class=\"callout-badge\">📖 GLOSSARY 核心名詞</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p class=\"semi-p\"><strong>📖 名詞｜中介層（Interposer）</strong></p>\n<ul class=\"semi-ul\"><li><strong>定義</strong>：放在晶片和封裝基板之間的一層轉接板，上面有細密的導線，讓多顆晶片之間能高速連接。</li><li><strong>現場用法</strong>：「這個產品的中介層超過一個曝光範圍，要用拼接的方式做。」</li><li><strong>相關名詞</strong>：2.5D、TSV、微凸塊、HBM</li><li><strong>常見混淆</strong>：中介層不一定是矽，也有使用有機材料，或只在晶片之間埋入一小塊矽橋的做法，成本和效能各有取捨。</li></ul></div></div>\n<p class=\"semi-p\">依中介層材質與互連結構，目前業界已知的 <strong>2.5D 封裝技術條例</strong>可歸類如下：</p>\n<div class=\"table-container\"><table class=\"semi-table\"><thead><tr><th>2.5D 子分類條例</th><th>已知代表技術與平台</th><th>結構特徵與典型應用</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>矽中介層（Silicon Interposer）</strong></td><td><strong>TSMC CoWoS-S</strong>、<strong>Samsung I-CubeS</strong>、<strong>UMC 2.5D Si Interposer</strong>、<strong>Amkor S-Connect</strong></td><td>採用整片單晶矽中介層（內含亞微米級高密度銅導線與 TSV 矽穿孔），可透過曝光拼接（Stitching）達 &gt; 3.3× 光罩面積；用於旗艦 AI/HPC GPU + HBM2E/3/3E 整合</td></tr><tr><td><strong>有機重佈線中介層（Organic RDL Interposer）</strong></td><td><strong>TSMC CoWoS-R</strong>、<strong>ASE FOCoS-CF / FOCoS-CL</strong>、<strong>Amkor S-SWIFT</strong></td><td>以多層有機高分子重佈線層（RDL）取代整片矽中介層，線寬／線距約 2 µm，具備極佳熱膨脹匹配與抗翹曲能力；用於高頻寬網通交換晶片與高性價比多晶片模組</td></tr><tr><td><strong>局部矽橋與重組中介層（Local Silicon Bridge）</strong></td><td><strong>TSMC CoWoS-L</strong>（LSI 局部矽互連）、<strong>Intel EMIB / EMIB-T</strong>、<strong>Samsung I-CubeE</strong>、<strong>ASE FOEB</strong></td><td>免除整片大尺寸矽晶圓，僅在相鄰晶片邊緣下方嵌入微型矽橋（Silicon Bridge，如 CoWoS-L 的 LSI 晶粒或基板內嵌的 EMIB；EMIB-T 並於矽橋加入 TSV），可擴展至 &gt; 5.5×～8× 光罩尺寸，成為次世代超大型 AI 加速器主力</td></tr><tr><td><strong>複合載板 2.5D（Hybrid Substrate）</strong></td><td><strong>Samsung H-Cube</strong>（Hybrid-Substrate Cube）</td><td>將精細線距 ABF 載板與高密度 HDI 基板上下疊合，在維持大面積封裝剛性的同時支撐多顆邏輯與 6～8 顆 HBM 並排整合</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<hr class=\"semi-hr\" />\n<h2 id=\"扇出型封裝\" class=\"heading-anchor\">扇出型封裝<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#扇出型封裝\" aria-hidden=\"true\">#</a></h2>\n<p class=\"semi-p\"><strong>扇出型封裝</strong>不使用傳統的基板：先把晶粒排列在一片承載板上，用封膠把它們包成一片「重組晶圓」，再在上面做出<strong>重佈線層</strong>（RDL），把接點從晶粒往外「扇」出去，擴展到比晶粒更大的面積。這種封裝又薄又小，常用在手機等輕薄的產品中。</p>\n<p class=\"semi-p\">扇出型封裝除平面擴展外，也發展出<strong>垂直堆疊的 3D 扇出封裝</strong>與<strong>晶圓級系統整合</strong>，已知主要條例包括：</p>\n<div class=\"table-container\"><table class=\"semi-table\"><thead><tr><th>扇出型與 3D 扇出條例</th><th>已知代表技術</th><th>結構特徵與典型應用</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>晶圓級平面扇出（FOWLP / InFO-RDL）</strong></td><td><strong>TSMC InFO-RDL</strong>、<strong>ASE FOWLP</strong>、<strong>Amkor SWIFT</strong></td><td>無載板薄型封裝，直接在重組晶圓表面建構高密度多層 RDL，大幅降低封裝厚度與寄生電感</td></tr><tr><td><strong>3D 扇出封裝體垂直堆疊（3D Fan-Out PoP / InFO-3D）</strong></td><td><strong>TSMC InFO-PoP</strong>、<strong>InFO_B</strong>、<strong>InFO-3D</strong>、<strong>Samsung ePoP / FO-PoP</strong></td><td>在底層扇出型應用處理器（AP）封裝四周製作<strong>貫穿封膠導通孔（Through-InFO Via, TIV / TMV）</strong>，將行動 LPDDR DRAM 垂直 3D 堆疊於上方，為旗艦智慧型手機處理器標準架構</td></tr><tr><td><strong>基板上扇出與面板級扇出（InFO-oS / FO-PLP）</strong></td><td><strong>TSMC InFO-oS / InFO_M</strong>、<strong>Samsung FO-PLP</strong>、<strong>ASE FO-EBG</strong>、<strong>PTI FOPLP</strong></td><td>將多顆小晶片透過扇出 RDL 互連後再安裝於封裝基板，或改在大面積矩形面板（Panel-Level，如 510×515 mm 至 600×600 mm）上製作以提升面積利用率</td></tr><tr><td><strong>晶圓級 3D 系統整合（System-on-Wafer）</strong></td><td><strong>TSMC InFO-SoW / CoW-SoW</strong></td><td>不將重組晶圓切單，直接在整片 300 mm 扇出晶圓上陣列整合數十顆高算力晶片，並在垂直方向直接接合供電與液冷散熱模組，用於超大規模 AI 訓練叢集</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<hr class=\"semi-hr\" />\n<h2 id=\"3d-堆疊往上疊\" class=\"heading-anchor\">3D 堆疊：往上疊<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#3d-堆疊往上疊\" aria-hidden=\"true\">#</a></h2>\n<p class=\"semi-p\"><strong>3D 堆疊</strong>把晶片直接疊在另一顆晶片上，透過 TSV 上下連通，HBM 就是一個例子。晶片之間的連接方式也在演進：</p>\n<div class=\"table-container\"><table class=\"semi-table\"><thead><tr><th>連接方式</th><th>接點間距</th><th>代表應用</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>覆晶凸塊</td><td>一百微米以上</td><td>一般的處理器封裝</td></tr><tr><td>微凸塊</td><td>數十微米</td><td>2.5D 封裝、HBM 堆疊</td></tr><tr><td>混合鍵合</td><td>十微米以下</td><td>高密度的 3D 晶片堆疊</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p class=\"semi-p\">接點間距越小，同樣面積內的連接點越多，晶片之間能傳輸的資料就越多。</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout-glossary\"><div class=\"callout-badge\">📖 GLOSSARY 核心名詞</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p class=\"semi-p\"><strong>📖 名詞｜混合鍵合（Hybrid Bonding）</strong></p>\n<ul class=\"semi-ul\"><li><strong>定義</strong>：不使用凸塊，讓兩顆晶片表面的銅接點直接接合，同時周圍的絕緣層也互相黏合的技術。</li><li><strong>現場用法</strong>：「改用混合鍵合之後，接點密度提高很多。」</li><li><strong>相關名詞</strong>：3D 堆疊、微凸塊、CMP、晶圓接合</li><li><strong>常見混淆</strong>：混合鍵合的「混合」，指的是金屬和絕緣層兩種材料同時接合，而不是混合使用兩種封裝方式。</li></ul></div></div>\n<p class=\"semi-p\">依照垂直互連機制（無凸塊混合鍵合、微凸塊／TSV 鍵合、記憶體垂直堆疊、以及 3D 結合 2.5D 的 3.5D 架構），目前半導體業界<strong>所有已知的 3D 封裝技術條例</strong>完整歸納如下：</p>\n<div class=\"table-container\"><table class=\"semi-table\"><thead><tr><th>3D 封裝條例分類</th><th>已知代表技術與子型號</th><th>接點間距與接合機制</th><th>代表架構與應用場景</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>條例 3A：無凸塊銅對銅混合鍵合（Bumpless Cu-Cu Hybrid Bonding）</strong></td><td>• <strong>TSMC SoIC-X</strong>（含 <strong>CoW</strong> 晶粒對晶圓、<strong>WoW</strong> 晶圓對晶圓）<br>• <strong>Intel Foveros Direct</strong><br>• <strong>Samsung X-Cube（Hybrid Bonding）</strong><br>• <strong>Samsung SAINT-S / SAINT-D / SAINT-L</strong><br>• <strong>3D NAND CBA</strong>（CMOS Bonded to Array）<br>• <strong>Sony 雙層／三層堆疊式 CIS</strong></td><td><strong>&lt; 10 µm 至 &lt; 1 µm</strong><br>（無焊錫凸塊、無底部填充膠；常溫 SiO₂-SiO₂ 親水分子鍵合 + 退火 Cu-Cu 原子擴散接合）</td><td>• <strong>SoIC-X / SAINT-S</strong>：SRAM 快取 3D 垂直堆疊於 CPU/GPU 上（如 AMD 3D V-Cache）<br>• <strong>SoIC-X / Foveros Direct / SAINT-L</strong>：邏輯疊邏輯（Logic-on-Logic）面對面（F2F）或面對背（F2B）超密互連<br>• <strong>SAINT-D</strong>：DRAM 與邏輯垂直整合<br>• <strong>CBA / CIS</strong>：晶圓對晶圓（W2W）將周邊 CMOS 與 3D NAND 陣列或像素／DRAM 晶圓三維疊合</td></tr><tr><td><strong>條例 3B：微凸塊與 TSV 垂直 3D 堆疊（Micro-Bump &amp; TSV 3D IC）</strong></td><td>• <strong>TSMC SoIC-P</strong>（Polymer / Micro-bump）<br>• <strong>Intel Foveros</strong>（標準 3D 面對面堆疊）<br>• <strong>Intel Foveros Omni</strong>（次世代全方位 3D 堆疊）<br>• <strong>Samsung X-Cube（µBump 微凸塊版）</strong><br>• <strong>ASE VIPack 3D IC</strong></td><td><strong>10 µm ～ 55 µm</strong><br>（以銅柱微凸塊 Cu Pillar Micro-bump 搭配熱壓鍵合 TCB、貫穿矽穿孔 TSV 與貫穿模塑穿孔 TMV）</td><td>• <strong>SoIC-P / X-Cube (µBump)</strong>：成本與良率最佳化的 3D 邏輯／快取垂直整合<br>• <strong>Foveros</strong>：將運算小晶片面對面疊在含 TSV 的主動基底晶粒（Active Base Die）上<br>• <strong>Foveros Omni</strong>：支援多顆頂層與多顆基底晶粒跨層拆解，搭配垂直銅柱直連供電</td></tr><tr><td><strong>條例 3C：3D 記憶體垂直堆疊（3D Memory Stacking）</strong></td><td>• <strong>HBM2E / HBM3 / HBM3E / HBM4</strong>（8H / 12H / 16H）<br>　├ <strong>TC-NCF</strong>（熱壓非導電膜）<br>　├ <strong>MR-MUF</strong>（巨量回焊模塑底部填膠）<br>　└ <strong>Hybrid Bonding / Fluxless HBM</strong><br>• <strong>3DS RDIMM</strong>（3D Stacked DDR5）<br>• <strong>CUBE / Custom 3D IoT DRAM</strong></td><td><strong>15 µm ～ 55 µm（微凸塊）</strong><br><strong>&lt; 10 µm（混合鍵合 HBM4+）</strong><br>（每顆薄化 DRAM 內含數千條 TSV 垂直貫穿，疊於 Base Logic Die 上）</td><td>• <strong>HBM</strong>：提供 1024-bit 至 2048-bit（HBM4）超寬介面與 &gt; 1～2 TB/s 單顆頻寬，為 AI 訓練／推論加速器核心記憶體<br>• <strong>3DS DRAM</strong>：以 TSV 將 2H/4H/8H DRAM 晶粒垂直封裝，倍增伺服器單條記憶體容量</td></tr><tr><td><strong>條例 3D：3.5D 複合異質整合（3D Stacking + 2.5D Interposer）</strong></td><td>• <strong>TSMC 3.5D（CoWoS-S/L + SoIC-X/P）</strong><br>• <strong>Intel Co-EMIB（Foveros + EMIB）</strong><br>• <strong>Samsung 3.5D（I-Cube / H-Cube + X-Cube / SAINT）</strong></td><td><strong>垂直 &lt; 1～9 µm（3D）</strong><br><strong>＋ 水平 25～40 µm（2.5D）</strong><br>（先向上 3D 堆疊，再橫向 2.5D 並排互連）</td><td>• 先以 <strong>3D SoIC / Foveros</strong> 將頂層運算核心、快取與底層 I/O 基底晶粒垂直疊合成 3D 超級晶粒，再透過 <strong>2.5D CoWoS-L 或 EMIB</strong> 與 8～12 顆 <strong>3D HBM</strong> 並排高速互連，兼顧垂直最短延遲與水平超大頻寬</td></tr><tr><td><strong>條例 3E：3D 光電共封裝與玻璃核心基板（3D CPO &amp; Glass Core TGV）</strong></td><td>• <strong>TSMC COUPE</strong>（Compact Universal Photonic Engine）<br>• <strong>Intel Silicon Photonics CPO</strong><br>• <strong>Broadcom Bailly SCIP</strong>、<strong>GF Fotonix</strong><br>• <strong>Glass Core Substrate + TGV</strong>（Intel / Samsung / Absolics / Ibiden）</td><td><strong>垂直 &lt; 10 µm Cu-Cu 鍵合（EIC-on-PIC）</strong><br><strong>＋ TGV 玻璃通孔（Pitch 40～100 µm）</strong><br>（電晶片 3D 疊於矽光子晶片上＋超平坦玻璃基板）</td><td>• <strong>COUPE / 3D CPO</strong>：以 SoIC-X 無凸塊混合鍵合將電子積體電路（EIC）垂直 3D 堆疊於矽光子積體電路（PIC）上，將電光轉換距離縮至數微米，突破 AI 叢集銅線 I/O 頻寬牆<br>• <strong>TGV 玻璃基板</strong>：以超平坦、低熱膨脹玻璃核心取代有機 ABF 核心，支撐 &gt; 100×100 mm² 超大型多光罩 3.5D 封裝</td></tr><tr><td><strong>條例 3F：單石 3D 積體電路與雙面 3D 晶圓整合（Monolithic 3D / CFET / BSPDN）</strong></td><td>• <strong>Sequential / Monolithic 3D IC</strong><br>• <strong>CFET（Complementary FET）</strong><br>• <strong>BSPDN（Intel PowerVia / TSMC SPR / Samsung BSPDN）</strong></td><td><strong>&lt; 100 nm 層間通孔（MIV / nTSV）</strong><br>（於單一晶圓內循序磊晶／鍵合多層電晶體，或利用晶圓正反兩面進行 3D 分工）</td><td>• <strong>Sequential 3D / CFET</strong>：直接在電晶體層級將 nMOS 與 pMOS 上下垂直 3D 堆疊，互連密度較 3D 封裝再高出 2～3 個數量級<br>• <strong>BSPDN</strong>：正面繞訊號、背面透過奈米穿矽通孔（nTSV）或背面直接接觸（SPR）垂直供電（詳見<a href=\"#ch12\" class=\"semi-link\">第 12 章</a>）</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p class=\"semi-p\">此外，在工程實務上，所有 <strong>3D 堆疊封裝</strong>皆會依照<strong>「晶片接合方向（Orientation）」</strong>與<strong>「接合對準粒度（Granularity）」</strong>兩大維度制定製程條例：</p>\n<div class=\"table-container\"><table class=\"semi-table\"><thead><tr><th>3D 鍵合拓撲與粒度條例</th><th>工程定義與連接路徑</th><th>優缺點與代表應用</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>面對面鍵合（F2F，Face-to-Face）</strong></td><td>上下兩顆晶粒的頂層金屬面（正面主動區）直接面對面接合；下層晶粒再透過 TSV 或凸塊連往基板</td><td>兩顆晶粒之間完全不需經過矽基板與 TSV，訊號路徑最短、寄生電容最小；廣泛用於雙層 <strong>SoIC-X F2F</strong>、<strong>Intel Foveros</strong> 與 <strong>3D NAND CBA</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>面對背鍵合（F2B，Face-to-Back）</strong>與<strong>背對背（B2B）</strong></td><td>上層晶粒正面接合至已減薄之下層晶粒背面，訊號必須藉由下層晶粒內部的 <strong>TSV（穿矽通孔）</strong> 垂直導通</td><td>可像蓋大樓一樣無限向上疊加第 3 層、第 8 層至第 16 層以上；為 <strong>HBM（8H/12H/16H）</strong>、<strong>3DS DRAM</strong> 與多層 <strong>SoIC / X-Cube</strong> 必備拓撲</td></tr><tr><td><strong>晶圓對晶圓鍵合（W2W，Wafer-to-Wafer）</strong></td><td>兩片完整 300 mm 晶圓直接整片對準與混合鍵合，再一次切割成 3D 堆疊晶粒</td><td>吞吐量極高、對準精度達 &lt; 200 nm；但上下晶粒面積必須完全相同，且無法預先剔除壞晶粒（良率相乘），適用於高良率之 <strong>Sony Stacked CIS</strong> 與 <strong>3D NAND CBA</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>晶粒對晶圓鍵合（D2W / CoW，Die-to-Wafer）</strong>與<strong>群組轉移（Collective D2W）</strong></td><td>先將上層晶圓切單並測試篩選出<strong>已知良好晶粒（KGD）</strong>，再逐顆或以載板群組方式貼合至底層晶圓（或中介層）上</td><td>允許上下層採用<strong>不同尺寸、不同製程節點</strong>的異質晶粒，且只把好晶粒疊上去以保全總良率；為 <strong>TSMC SoIC-X (CoW)</strong>、<strong>Intel Foveros Direct / Omni</strong> 與 <strong>HBM</strong> 主力做法</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<hr class=\"semi-hr\" />\n<h2 id=\"小晶片chiplet\" class=\"heading-anchor\">小晶片（Chiplet）<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#小晶片chiplet\" aria-hidden=\"true\">#</a></h2>\n<p class=\"semi-p\">把一顆大型晶片拆成多顆功能獨立的小晶片，再封裝在一起，這種設計方式稱為 <strong>Chiplet</strong>。產業也在推動晶片之間互相連接的標準介面，目標是讓不同來源的小晶片能像積木一樣組合使用。</p>\n<p class=\"semi-p\">隨著先進封裝大量使用微影、電鍍、CMP 等原本屬於晶圓廠的製程，前段製造和後段封裝之間的界線也越來越模糊。</p>\n<div class=\"table-container\"><table class=\"semi-table\"><thead><tr><th>小晶片（Chiplet）互連標準條例</th><th>適用封裝層級（2D / 2.5D / 3D）</th><th>關鍵規格與產業角色</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>UCIe（Universal Chiplet Interconnect Express）</strong><br>（含 <strong>UCIe-Standard</strong>、<strong>UCIe-Advanced</strong>、<strong>UCIe-3D</strong>）</td><td>• <strong>UCIe-Standard</strong>：有機基板（100–130 µm 凸塊）<br>• <strong>UCIe-Advanced</strong>：2.5D CoWoS / EMIB（25–55 µm 微凸塊）<br>• <strong>UCIe-3D</strong>：3D SoIC / Foveros Direct（&lt; 10 µm 至次微米混合鍵合）</td><td>跨晶圓代工、IC 設計與雲端大廠的開放通用標準，定義物理層（PHY）、協定層與軟體堆疊，支援 PCIe / CXL 協定與跨生態系小晶片隨插即用</td></tr><tr><td><strong>AIB（Advanced Interface Bus）</strong>與 <strong>BoW（Bunch of Wires）</strong></td><td>2D 有機載板、2.5D 矽橋（EMIB）與中介層封裝</td><td>採用高密度短距離平行單端訊號（如類 DDR 時脈轉發架構），以極簡電路面積提供高頻寬、低延遲晶粒互連</td></tr><tr><td><strong>專屬高速架構互連（NVLink-C2C / Infinity Fabric 2.5D &amp; 3D）</strong></td><td>2.5D CoWoS-S/L、3D SoIC 垂直堆疊與 3.5D 複合封裝</td><td>針對特定 AI 超算與 CPU+GPU 記憶體一致性（Cache-Coherent）叢集最佳化之超高速互連介面</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"callout callout-knowhow\"><div class=\"callout-badge\">🔧 FAB KNOW-HOW 現場實務</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p class=\"semi-p\"><strong>🔧 Know-how｜一顆壞晶片，拖垮整個封裝</strong></p>\n<ul class=\"semi-ul\"><li><strong>情境</strong>：一個先進封裝裡放了八顆晶片。</li><li><strong>做法</strong>：每一顆晶片在封裝前都要經過充分測試，確保是已知良好晶粒（KGD），封裝過程中也盡量安排可以檢查的步驟。</li><li><strong>為什麼</strong>：良率會相乘。就算每顆晶片的良率都是 99%，八顆全部都好的機率也只剩大約 92%。</li><li><strong>沒做會怎樣</strong>：只要一顆晶片有問題，整個昂貴的封裝連同其他好晶片都一起報廢。</li><li><strong>相關章節</strong>：<a href=\"#ch19\" class=\"semi-link\">第 19 章 晶圓測試</a></li></ul>\n<p class=\"semi-p\"><strong>🔧 Know-how｜混合鍵合需要前段等級的乾淨和平坦</strong></p>\n<ul class=\"semi-ul\"><li><strong>情境</strong>：兩顆晶片要用混合鍵合直接接合。</li><li><strong>做法</strong>：接合面要經過極精密的 CMP，接合前的清洗和環境控制也要達到晶圓廠的等級。</li><li><strong>為什麼</strong>：兩個表面之間沒有凸塊可以緩衝，一顆微粒就會撐出一個空隙，表面稍微不平也會接合不良。</li><li><strong>沒做會怎樣</strong>：一顆微粒可能讓周圍大量接點同時失效。</li><li><strong>相關章節</strong>：<a href=\"#ch08\" class=\"semi-link\">第 8 章 CMP</a>、<a href=\"#ch09\" class=\"semi-link\">第 9 章 清洗與污染控制</a></li></ul></div></div>\n<hr class=\"semi-hr\" />\n<h2 id=\"先進封裝的挑戰\" class=\"heading-anchor\">先進封裝的挑戰<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#先進封裝的挑戰\" aria-hidden=\"true\">#</a></h2>\n<div class=\"table-container\"><table class=\"semi-table\"><thead><tr><th>挑戰</th><th>說明</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>散熱</td><td>晶片緊密排列或疊在一起，熱更難散出去</td></tr><tr><td>翹曲</td><td>不同材料受熱膨脹的程度不同，封裝越大越容易彎曲</td></tr><tr><td>測試</td><td>晶片疊起來之後，中間的晶片很難再單獨測試</td></tr><tr><td>良率相乘</td><td>任何一顆晶片或一個接點失敗，整個封裝都受影響</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<hr class=\"semi-hr\" />\n<h2 id=\"已知25d扇出型與3d封裝條例總覽\" class=\"heading-anchor\">2.5D、扇出型與 3D／3.5D 封裝條例總覽<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#已知25d扇出型與3d封裝條例總覽\" aria-hidden=\"true\">#</a></h2>\n<div class=\"table-container\"><table class=\"semi-table\"><thead><tr><th>3D / 2.5D 封裝工程挑戰</th><th>物理瓶頸機制</th><th>現行工程對策與標準條例</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>3D 跨層熱阻與熱點耦合（Thermal Coupling）</strong></td><td>多層晶片垂直疊合後，底層高功耗邏輯晶片的熱量被上方快取或 HBM 阻擋，且微凸塊／底部填膠導熱率遠低於單晶矽</td><td>導入<strong>結構填充矽（Dummy / Structural Silicon）</strong>、無凸塊 Cu-Cu 混合鍵合降低介面熱阻、<strong>液態金屬／銦片（Indium TIM1）</strong>、直觸式液冷板（Cold Plate）與晶圓內微流道散熱</td></tr><tr><td><strong>大面積翹曲與晶片封裝交互作用（Warpage &amp; CPI）</strong></td><td>矽（CTE ≈ 2.6 ppm/K）、銅（16.5 ppm/K）與有機 ABF 載板（14–17 ppm/K）熱膨脹落差，在回焊高溫與室溫間造成哭臉／笑臉彎曲甚至撕裂晶片內脆弱的 Low-k 介電層</td><td>採用封裝金屬補強環（Stiffener Ring）、模塑底部填充（MR-MUF）、有機／局部矽橋中介層（CoWoS-R/L），並邁向<strong>次世代玻璃核心基板（TGV Glass Core，CTE 可調配對齊矽）</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>3D 堆疊內部可測性與通道修復（3D DFT &amp; Repair）</strong></td><td>晶粒一旦透過微凸塊或混合鍵合疊合封死，探針即無法直接接觸中間層晶粒焊墊</td><td>全面導入 <strong>IEEE 1838 3D 堆疊測試標準</strong>（定義 PTAP 主測試存取埠、STAP 次級埠與 FPP 高速彈性平行埠），並搭配 <strong>UCIe / HBM 內建冗餘 TSV 與自動備援通道修復（Lane Repair）</strong></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<hr class=\"semi-hr\" />\n<h2 id=\"定量物理定律與3d製程視窗\" class=\"heading-anchor\">定量物理定律與 3D 製程視窗<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#定量物理定律與3d製程視窗\" aria-hidden=\"true\">#</a></h2>\n<p class=\"semi-p\">在 2.5D（CoWoS / EMIB）、扇出型（InFO / FOPLP）與 <strong>3D／3.5D 無凸塊混合鍵合（SoIC / Foveros Direct / HBM / TGV 玻璃基板）</strong>中，三大定量物理缩放定律如下：</p>\n<div class=\"table-container\"><table class=\"semi-table\"><thead><tr><th>2.5D/3D 異質整合定量定律</th><th>核心數學關係式</th><th>跨世代物理標尺對比</th><th>對 AI 算力系統、CPO 光電共封裝與玻璃基板之決定性意義</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td><strong>互連節距平方反比密度律與每位元傳輸能耗方程（Pitch $1/P^2$ &amp; Energy-per-Bit Law）</strong></td><td>$D_{\\text{IO}} = \\frac{1}{P_{\\text{pitch}}^2},\\quad E_{\\text{bit}} = \\frac{1}{2} C_{\\text{io}} V_{\\text{swing}}^2$</td><td>由傳統覆晶（$P=150\\ \\mu\\text{m} \\to 44\\text{ IO/mm}^2$，$E_{\\text{bit}} \\sim 5\\text{ pJ/bit}$）$\\rightarrow$ 2.5D 微凸塊（$P=36\\ \\mu\\text{m} \\to 770\\text{ IO/mm}^2$，$\\sim 0.5\\text{ pJ/bit}$）$\\rightarrow$ <strong>3D 混合鍵合（$P=3\\ \\mu\\text{m} \\to 1.1\\times 10^5\\text{ IO/mm}^2$，$E_{\\text{bit}} &lt; 0.05\\text{ pJ/bit}$）</strong></td><td>節距縮小 10 倍，面積互連密度即暴增 $10^2 = 100$ 倍！使上下堆疊的 3D 小晶片能以如同單一晶片內部金屬線的極低延遲與極低功耗進行 TB/s 級通訊</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>多層 3D 垂直堆疊熱阻疊加耦合矩陣（3D Stacked IC Thermal Coupling Law）</strong></td><td>$T_{j,k} = T_{\\text{coolant}} + \\sum_{m=1}^{N} R_{\\text{th},km}\\,P_m,\\quad \\Delta T_{\\text{3D}} \\propto \\sum_{k=1}^{N} P_k \\left(\\sum_{i=k}^{N} \\frac{t_i}{\\kappa_i A}\\right)$</td><td>在 $N$ 層垂直堆疊（如 SRAM/Logic 疊合或 12/16-Hi HBM）中，底層裸晶的發熱必須穿透上方所有裸晶與鍵合界面才能傳至頂部散熱器，形成跨層自熱耦合（Cross-Heating）</td><td>推動兩大 3D 散熱革命：① 將高功耗運算層放在<strong>最靠近頂部水冷板的上層</strong>；② 以無有機膠之 <code>Cu-Cu / SiO₂ 直接混合鍵合</code> 與 <code>結構矽／微流道直冷</code> 消除界面熱障</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>Stoney 雙材料熱應力翹曲與大尺寸基板曲率方程（Stoney Warpage Scaling Law）</strong></td><td>$\\kappa_{\\text{warp}} = \\frac{1}{R} = \\frac{6 E_f t_f (\\alpha_f - \\alpha_s)\\Delta T}{(1-\\nu_s) E_s t_s^2},\\quad w_{\\text{max}} \\approx \\frac{L_{\\text{pkg}}^2}{8 R}$</td><td>封裝體最大翹曲高度 $w_{\\text{max}}$ 與封裝邊長平方 $L_{\\text{pkg}}^2$ 成正比，與基板楊氏模數 $E_s$ 及厚度平方 $t_s^2$ 成反比</td><td>當 CoWoS-L 封裝尺寸突破 $100\\times 100\\text{ mm}^2$（8–12 倍光罩面積）時，有機基板在回焊高溫下嚴重翹曲（Smile/Cry），直接催生高剛性、CTE 可調（<code>3–9 ppm/K</code>）的<strong>次世代玻璃核心基板（TGV Glass Core Substrate）</strong></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<hr class=\"semi-hr\" />\n<h2 id=\"現場異常徵兆與跨站根因排查\" class=\"heading-anchor\">現場異常徵兆與跨站根因排查<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#現場異常徵兆與跨站根因排查\" aria-hidden=\"true\">#</a></h2>\n<p class=\"semi-p\">2.5D/3D 先進封裝將單體面積推向數倍光罩極限並把百瓦熱源垂直疊在一起：<strong>大型 CoWoS 雙向哭笑臉熱翹曲導致微凸塊虛焊、3D SoIC 混合鍵合奈米微粒空洞，以及 3D 垂直熱耦合降速</strong>為三大核心異常：</p>\n<div class=\"table-container\"><table class=\"semi-table\"><thead><tr><th>現場異常徵兆與晶圓圖／電性特徵</th><th>底層物理與製程失效根因（Root Cause）</th><th>跨站排查與在線量測／FA 驗證手法</th><th>OCAP 緊急防堵與永久防呆對策</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td><strong>大型 CoWoS / 2.5D 封裝在室溫與迴焊高溫間發生「哭臉／笑臉」翹曲反轉導致空焊與橋接（Smile/Cry Warpage Non-Wet Open &amp; Bridging）</strong></td><td>在 $> 3\\times$ 光罩面積的巨型封裝中，室溫下矽晶片與載板收縮不均呈現中央拱起的「哭臉（Cry / Convex）」；升溫至 $250^\\circ\\text{C}$ 迴焊時則反轉為邊緣翹起的「笑臉（Smile / Concave）」；若動態翹曲超過 $> 120\\text{ }\\mu\\text{m}$，中央錫球被壓扁橋接（SBL），四角錫球則懸空拉斷成不沾錫開路（Non-Wet Open, NWO）</td><td>使用 <strong>陰影疊紋干涉儀（Shadow Moiré）</strong> 量測 $25^\\circ\\text{C} \\rightarrow 260^\\circ\\text{C} \\rightarrow 25^\\circ\\text{C}$ 全溫程三維翹曲動態曲面，並以 3D X-Ray 檢查頭枕效應（Head-in-Pillow, HiP）與 NWO</td><td>在載板四邊加裝 <strong>高剛性不鏽鋼／銅防翹曲補強環（Stiffener Ring）</strong>、調整環氧模封膠（EMC）玻璃轉移溫度 $T_g$，並在超大尺寸封裝導入 <strong>低膨脹玻璃核心基板（Glass Core Substrate）</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>3D SoIC / 混合鍵合界面因單顆 50nm 微粒撐開毫米級圓形未鍵合空洞（Hybrid Bond Particle Blister Void）</strong></td><td>無凸塊銅對銅混合鍵合要求表面粗糙度 $R_q &lt; 0.2\\text{ nm}$；根據彈性力學薄板能量平衡定律，界面只要夾入一顆直徑僅 $50\\text{ nm}$ 的硬質微粒，就會把上下高剛性矽晶圓撐開直徑達 $0.5\\text{–}2\\text{ mm}$ 的圓形帳篷狀未鍵合氣泡（Blister Void），切斷內部數千個銅接點</td><td>在室溫預鍵合後、高溫退火前，立即執行 <strong>100% 全晶圓高頻 C-SAM 超音波或紅外線干涉掃描</strong>，定位所有直徑 $> 100\\text{ }\\mu\\text{m}$ 之圓形干涉牛頓環空洞</td><td>將混合鍵合機設置於 <strong>ISO Class 1 極淨微環境</strong>，在貼合前數秒內於同一機台內連續執行 <strong>去離子臭氧水（$\\text{DIO}_3$）兆赫超音波刷洗 + $\\text{N}_2/\\text{O}_2$ 電漿親水活化</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>3D 垂直堆疊底層邏輯高熱流直接烘烤頂層 SRAM / HBM 引發熱降頻與微裂（3D Thermal Cross-Heating &amp; TIM Delamination）</strong></td><td>在 3D 堆疊中，底層高功耗運算晶粒（熱通量 $> 1.5\\text{ W/mm}^2$）的熱量必須穿過高熱阻的層間鍵合介電質或微凸塊底膠才能抵達頂部均熱片，導致頂層 3D V-Cache 或旁側 HBM 接合溫度 $T_j$ 突破 $95^\\circ\\text{C}$ 上限</td><td>透過片上數十顆數位熱感測器（DTS）繪製三維瞬態溫度場，並以超音波檢查液態金屬／相變化導熱介面材料（TIM）在熱循環後的幫浦擠出效應（Pump-Out Void）</td><td>在 3D 結構空白處填滿 <strong>高導熱結構矽晶片（Structural Thermal Dummy Silicon）與導熱矽穿孔（Thermal TSV）</strong>，頂部背面採用 <strong>銦片軟焊導熱層（Indium Metallic TIM）或直接液冷微流道上蓋（Microchannel Direct Liquid Cold Plate）</strong></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<hr class=\"semi-hr\" />\n<h2 id=\"本章重點\" class=\"heading-anchor\">本章重點<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#本章重點\" aria-hidden=\"true\">#</a></h2>\n<ol class=\"semi-ol\"><li>微縮越來越難，先進封裝成為提升效能的新方向。</li><li>2.5D 封裝把多顆晶片並排在中介層上，常見於處理器加 HBM。</li><li>扇出型封裝用重佈線層把接點往外擴展，適合輕薄產品。</li><li>3D 堆疊從微凸塊走向混合鍵合，接點密度越來越高。</li><li>良率會相乘，所以每顆晶片都必須是已知良好晶粒。</li></ol>\n<hr class=\"semi-hr\" />\n<h2 id=\"延伸閱讀\" class=\"heading-anchor\">延伸閱讀<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#延伸閱讀\" aria-hidden=\"true\">#</a></h2>\n<ul class=\"semi-ul\"><li>John H. Lau，《Semiconductor Advanced Packaging》</li><li>IEEE ECTC（Electronic Components and Technology Conference）歷年論文</li></ul>\n<hr class=\"semi-hr\" />\n<p class=\"semi-p\"><a href=\"#ch20\" class=\"semi-link\">← 上一章：第 20 章 封裝</a> ｜ <a href=\"#explore\" class=\"semi-link\">目錄</a> ｜ <a href=\"#ch22\" class=\"semi-link\">下一章：第 22 章 最終測試與可靠度 →</a></p>","contentHtmlEn":"<p class=\"semi-p\"><!-- source: zh-TW/5-backend/21-advanced-packaging/README.md | sha: 75fadd628f59 --></p>\n<h1 id=\"chapter-21-advanced-packaging-integrating-multiple-chips-into-one\" class=\"heading-anchor\">Chapter 21: Advanced Packaging — Integrating Multiple Chips into One<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#chapter-21-advanced-packaging-integrating-multiple-chips-into-one\" aria-hidden=\"true\">#</a></h1>\n<div class=\"callout callout-wafer-pos\"><div class=\"callout-badge\">📍 WAFER TRACK</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p class=\"semi-p\">📍 <strong>Where the wafer is</strong></p>\n<ul class=\"semi-ul\"><li>Previous stop: wafer test, the good dies have been identified</li><li><strong>This chapter: advanced packaging, integrating several chips into one system</strong></li><li>Next stop: final test</li></ul></div></div>\n<hr class=\"semi-hr\" />\n<h2 id=\"why-advanced-packaging-is-needed\" class=\"heading-anchor\">Why advanced packaging is needed<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#why-advanced-packaging-is-needed\" aria-hidden=\"true\">#</a></h2>\n<p class=\"semi-p\">In the past, chip performance improved mainly by shrinking transistors. But that road is getting harder and more expensive, and it runs into several limits:</p>\n<ul class=\"semi-ul\"><li><strong>A die cannot grow without limit</strong>: The size of a die is limited by the area a scanner can expose at once, about 26 mm × 33 mm.</li><li><strong>Large dies have low yield</strong>: As Chapter 16 explained, the bigger the die, the more likely it is to be hit by a defect.</li><li><strong>Different functions suit different processes</strong>: Compute cores benefit from the most advanced process, analog and I/O circuits are fine on mature processes, and memory needs its own dedicated process.</li><li><strong>Bandwidth demand has exploded</strong>: AI computing needs to move huge amounts of data between processors and memory.</li></ul>\n<p class=\"semi-p\">So the industry started splitting one large chip into several smaller chips, making each with the process that suits it best, and then integrating them tightly with advanced packaging so they work like a single chip. Packaging is no longer just \"protection\"; it has become key to performance.</p>\n<hr class=\"semi-hr\" />\n<h2 id=\"25d-side-by-side-on-an-interposer\" class=\"heading-anchor\">2.5D: side by side on an interposer<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#25d-side-by-side-on-an-interposer\" aria-hidden=\"true\">#</a></h2>\n<p class=\"semi-p\"><strong>2.5D packaging</strong> places several chips side by side on an <strong>interposer</strong>. The interposer is usually a piece of silicon with very fine, dense wiring that lets the chips communicate with each other quickly and in large volumes. The interposer then connects to the package substrate below through TSVs.</p>\n<p class=\"semi-p\">The classic example places a processor and several stacks of HBM memory side by side on the same interposer. The interposer can even be made larger than a single exposure field by stitching several exposures together.</p>\n<p class=\"semi-p\"><!-- Figure: cross-section of a 2.5D package (processor and HBM side by side on an interposer, with the substrate below) --></p>\n<div class=\"callout callout-glossary\"><div class=\"callout-badge\">📖 GLOSSARY & KEY TERMS</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p class=\"semi-p\"><strong>📖 Term | Interposer (中介層)</strong></p>\n<ul class=\"semi-ul\"><li><strong>Definition</strong>: An adapter layer placed between the chips and the package substrate, with fine, dense wiring that lets several chips connect at high speed.</li><li><strong>On the floor</strong>: \"The interposer for this product is bigger than one exposure field, so it has to be stitched.\"</li><li><strong>Related terms</strong>: 2.5D, TSV, micro bump, HBM</li><li><strong>Common confusion</strong>: An interposer is not always silicon. Some use organic materials, and some only embed small silicon bridges between the chips. Each option trades off cost and performance.</li></ul></div></div>\n<p class=\"semi-p\">Based on interposer material and bridge topology, all known mainstream <strong>2.5D packaging technologies</strong> are categorized under the following clauses:</p>\n<div class=\"table-container\"><table class=\"semi-table\"><thead><tr><th>2.5D Sub-Clause</th><th>Known Technologies &amp; Platforms</th><th>Structural Features &amp; Typical Applications</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Monolithic Silicon Interposer</strong></td><td><strong>TSMC CoWoS-S</strong>, <strong>Samsung I-CubeS</strong>, <strong>UMC 2.5D Si Interposer</strong>, <strong>Amkor S-Connect</strong></td><td>Uses a full silicon interposer with sub-micron damascene wiring and TSVs, reticle-stitched beyond &gt;3.3× reticle size; standard for flagship AI/HPC GPUs + HBM2E/3/3E</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Organic RDL Interposer</strong></td><td><strong>TSMC CoWoS-R</strong>, <strong>ASE FOCoS-CF / FOCoS-CL</strong>, <strong>Amkor S-SWIFT</strong></td><td>Replaces the silicon interposer with multi-layer organic polymer redistribution layers (~2 µm L/S), offering low warpage and high thermal-mechanical reliability for networking and multi-die SoCs</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Local Silicon Bridge &amp; Reconstituted Interposer</strong></td><td><strong>TSMC CoWoS-L</strong> (LSI bridges), <strong>Intel EMIB / EMIB-T</strong>, <strong>Samsung I-CubeE</strong>, <strong>ASE FOEB</strong></td><td>Embeds tiny silicon bridges (Local Silicon Interconnect [LSI] dies in reconstituted mold or EMIB bridges inside organic substrates; EMIB-T adds TSVs to bridges) only where die-to-die high-density links are needed, scaling past 5.5×–8× reticle size</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Hybrid-Substrate 2.5D</strong></td><td><strong>Samsung H-Cube</strong> (Hybrid-Substrate Cube)</td><td>Splits the substrate into a fine-pitch ABF upper tier and an HDI lower tier to support large-area multi-HBM integration with controlled warpage</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<hr class=\"semi-hr\" />\n<h2 id=\"fan-out-packaging\" class=\"heading-anchor\">Fan-out packaging<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#fan-out-packaging\" aria-hidden=\"true\">#</a></h2>\n<p class=\"semi-p\"><strong>Fan-out packaging</strong> does not use a traditional substrate. The dies are first arranged on a carrier and encapsulated in mold compound to form a \"reconstituted wafer.\" A <strong>redistribution layer</strong> (RDL) is then built on top, spreading the contacts \"out\" from the die to an area larger than the die itself. These packages are thin and small, and they are common in thin, light products such as phones.</p>\n<p class=\"semi-p\">Beyond planar fan-out, the technology spans <strong>3D Fan-Out vertical package stacking</strong> and <strong>wafer-scale systems</strong>, organized into the following known clauses:</p>\n<div class=\"table-container\"><table class=\"semi-table\"><thead><tr><th>Fan-Out &amp; 3D Fan-Out Clause</th><th>Known Technologies</th><th>Structural Features &amp; Typical Applications</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Wafer-Level Planar Fan-Out (FOWLP)</strong></td><td><strong>TSMC InFO-RDL</strong>, <strong>ASE FOWLP</strong>, <strong>Amkor SWIFT</strong></td><td>Substrate-less ultra-thin package with multi-layer fine-line RDL built directly on a reconstituted wafer</td></tr><tr><td><strong>3D Fan-Out Package Stacking (InFO-PoP / InFO-3D)</strong></td><td><strong>TSMC InFO-PoP</strong>, <strong>InFO_B</strong>, <strong>InFO-3D</strong>, <strong>Samsung FO-PoP</strong></td><td>Forms vertical <strong>Through-InFO Vias (TIV / TMV)</strong> around the bottom fan-out logic die to stack mobile LPDDR DRAM packages in 3D directly on top; ubiquitous in flagship smartphone SoCs</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Fan-Out on Substrate &amp; Panel-Level (InFO-oS / FO-PLP)</strong></td><td><strong>TSMC InFO-oS / InFO_M</strong>, <strong>Samsung FO-PLP</strong>, <strong>ASE FO-EBG</strong>, <strong>PTI FOPLP</strong></td><td>Mounts multi-die fan-out modules onto a substrate, or processes reconstituted rectangular panels (510×515 mm to 600×600 mm) for higher area utilization</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Wafer-Scale 3D System Integration (System-on-Wafer)</strong></td><td><strong>TSMC InFO-SoW / CoW-SoW</strong></td><td>Integrates dozens of compute dies across an entire uncut 300 mm reconstituted wafer with vertical power delivery and liquid cooling for AI supercomputers</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<hr class=\"semi-hr\" />\n<h2 id=\"3d-stacking-building-upward\" class=\"heading-anchor\">3D stacking: building upward<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#3d-stacking-building-upward\" aria-hidden=\"true\">#</a></h2>\n<p class=\"semi-p\"><strong>3D stacking</strong> places chips directly on top of other chips and connects them vertically through TSVs. HBM is one example. The way chips are connected to each other keeps evolving:</p>\n<div class=\"table-container\"><table class=\"semi-table\"><thead><tr><th>Connection method</th><th>Contact pitch</th><th>Typical use</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Flip-chip bumps</td><td>A hundred micrometers or more</td><td>Ordinary processor packages</td></tr><tr><td>Micro bumps</td><td>Tens of micrometers</td><td>2.5D packages, HBM stacks</td></tr><tr><td>Hybrid bonding</td><td>Below ten micrometers</td><td>High-density 3D chip stacking</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p class=\"semi-p\">The smaller the contact pitch, the more connections fit in the same area, and the more data can move between the chips.</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout-glossary\"><div class=\"callout-badge\">📖 GLOSSARY & KEY TERMS</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p class=\"semi-p\"><strong>📖 Term | Hybrid bonding (混合鍵合)</strong></p>\n<ul class=\"semi-ul\"><li><strong>Definition</strong>: A technique that bonds the copper contacts on two chip surfaces directly, without bumps, while the surrounding insulating layers also bond to each other.</li><li><strong>On the floor</strong>: \"Since we moved to hybrid bonding, the connection density has gone way up.\"</li><li><strong>Related terms</strong>: 3D stacking, micro bump, CMP, wafer bonding</li><li><strong>Common confusion</strong>: The \"hybrid\" in hybrid bonding means that two kinds of material, metal and insulator, bond at the same time. It does not mean mixing two packaging methods.</li></ul></div></div>\n<p class=\"semi-p\">Organized by vertical interconnect mechanism—bumpless hybrid bonding, micro-bump/TSV stacking, 3D memory stacking, and 3.5D hybrid topology—<strong>all known 3D packaging technologies</strong> in the industry are classified under the following four clauses:</p>\n<div class=\"table-container\"><table class=\"semi-table\"><thead><tr><th>3D Packaging Clause</th><th>Known Technologies &amp; Sub-Variants</th><th>Contact Pitch &amp; Bonding Mechanism</th><th>Representative Architecture &amp; Applications</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Clause 3A: Bumpless Cu-Cu Hybrid Bonding 3D IC</strong></td><td>• <strong>TSMC SoIC-X</strong> (<strong>CoW</strong> Chip-on-Wafer &amp; <strong>WoW</strong> Wafer-on-Wafer)<br>• <strong>Intel Foveros Direct</strong><br>• <strong>Samsung X-Cube (Hybrid Bonding)</strong><br>• <strong>Samsung SAINT-S / SAINT-D / SAINT-L</strong><br>• <strong>3D NAND CBA</strong> (CMOS Bonded to Array)<br>• <strong>Sony 2-Layer / 3-Layer Stacked CIS</strong></td><td><strong>&lt; 10 µm down to &lt; 1 µm</strong><br>(Zero solder bumps, zero underfill; room-temp SiO₂-SiO₂ hydrophilic oxide bonding + thermal anneal Cu-Cu atomic diffusion)</td><td>• <strong>SoIC-X / SAINT-S</strong>: 3D vertical SRAM cache on CPU/GPU logic (e.g., AMD 3D V-Cache)<br>• <strong>SoIC-X / Foveros Direct / SAINT-L</strong>: Face-to-Face (F2F) or Face-to-Back (F2B) Logic-on-Logic stacking<br>• <strong>SAINT-D</strong>: Vertical DRAM-on-Logic 3D integration<br>• <strong>CBA / CIS</strong>: Wafer-to-Wafer (W2W) bonding of CMOS logic wafers to 3D NAND arrays or pixel/DRAM wafers</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Clause 3B: Micro-Bump &amp; TSV Vertical 3D IC</strong></td><td>• <strong>TSMC SoIC-P</strong> (Polymer / Micro-bump)<br>• <strong>Intel Foveros</strong> (Standard F2F 3D Stacking)<br>• <strong>Intel Foveros Omni</strong> (Disaggregated 3D)<br>• <strong>Samsung X-Cube (µBump variant)</strong><br>• <strong>ASE VIPack 3D IC</strong></td><td><strong>10 µm – 55 µm</strong><br>(Cu-pillar micro-bumps with Thermo-Compression Bonding [TCB], Through-Silicon Vias [TSVs], and Through-Mold Vias [TMVs])</td><td>• <strong>SoIC-P / X-Cube (µBump)</strong>: Cost-optimized 3D vertical stacking for logic and cache<br>• <strong>Foveros</strong>: Stacks compute chiplets face-to-face onto an active TSV base die<br>• <strong>Foveros Omni</strong>: Supports arbitrary multi-top-die to multi-base-die disaggregation with direct through-mold copper columns</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Clause 3C: 3D Memory Vertical Stacking</strong></td><td>• <strong>HBM2E / HBM3 / HBM3E / HBM4</strong> (8H / 12H / 16H)<br>　├ <strong>TC-NCF</strong> (Thermal Compression + NCF)<br>　├ <strong>MR-MUF</strong> (Mass Reflow Molded Underfill)<br>　└ <strong>Hybrid Bonding / Fluxless HBM</strong><br>• <strong>3DS RDIMM</strong> (3D Stacked DDR5)<br>• <strong>Custom 3D Cube DRAM</strong></td><td><strong>15 µm – 55 µm (Micro-bump)</strong><br><strong>&lt; 10 µm (Hybrid Bonding HBM4+)</strong><br>(Thousands of TSVs pierce thinned DRAM core dies stacked atop a Base Logic Die)</td><td>• <strong>HBM</strong>: Delivers 1024-bit to 2048-bit (HBM4) ultra-wide interfaces and &gt;1–2 TB/s per stack for AI accelerators<br>• <strong>3DS DRAM</strong>: Vertically stacks 2H/4H/8H DDR5 dies via TSVs for high-capacity server memory</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Clause 3D: 3.5D Hybrid Integration (3D + 2.5D)</strong></td><td>• <strong>TSMC 3.5D (CoWoS-S/L + SoIC-X/P)</strong><br>• <strong>Intel Co-EMIB (Foveros + EMIB)</strong><br>• <strong>Samsung 3.5D (I-Cube / H-Cube + X-Cube / SAINT)</strong></td><td><strong>Vertical &lt; 1–9 µm (3D)</strong><br><strong>+ Lateral 25–40 µm (2.5D)</strong><br>(Combines vertical 3D die stacking with lateral 2.5D interposer/bridge routing)</td><td>• Vertically stacks compute cores, SRAM cache, and base I/O dies via <strong>3D SoIC / Foveros</strong>, then mounts multiple 3D stacks alongside 8–12 <strong>3D HBM</strong> modules onto a <strong>2.5D CoWoS-L or EMIB</strong> platform</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Clause 3E: 3D Co-Packaged Optics (CPO) &amp; Glass Core Substrate (TGV)</strong></td><td>• <strong>TSMC COUPE</strong> (Compact Universal Photonic Engine)<br>• <strong>Intel Silicon Photonics CPO</strong><br>• <strong>Broadcom Bailly SCIP</strong>, <strong>GF Fotonix</strong><br>• <strong>Glass Core Substrate + TGV</strong> (Intel / Samsung / Absolics / Ibiden)</td><td><strong>Vertical &lt; 10 µm Cu-Cu Bonding (EIC-on-PIC)</strong><br><strong>+ Through-Glass Vias (TGV, 40–100 µm pitch)</strong></td><td>• <strong>COUPE / 3D CPO</strong>: Uses SoIC-X bumpless hybrid bonding to stack the Electrical IC (EIC) directly atop the Silicon Photonic IC (PIC), slashing electrical trace loss for optical AI scale-up fabrics<br>• <strong>TGV Glass Core</strong>: Ultra-flat, low-CTE glass core replaces organic ABF core to support &gt;100×100 mm² multi-reticle 3.5D packages without warpage</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Clause 3F: Monolithic 3D IC &amp; Wafer-Backside 3D Integration (CFET / BSPDN)</strong></td><td>• <strong>Sequential / Monolithic 3D IC</strong><br>• <strong>CFET (Complementary FET)</strong><br>• <strong>BSPDN (Intel PowerVia / TSMC SPR / Samsung BSPDN)</strong></td><td><strong>&lt; 100 nm Monolithic Inter-tier Vias (MIV / nTSV)</strong><br>(Device-tier vertical stacking or dual-sided wafer integration)</td><td>• <strong>Sequential 3D / CFET</strong>: Stacks nMOS and pMOS transistor tiers vertically with nanoscale MIVs, boosting interconnect density 100× beyond die-level 3D packaging<br>• <strong>BSPDN</strong>: Separates frontside signal routing from backside power delivery via nano-TSVs or direct backside contacts (see <a href=\"#ch12\" class=\"semi-link\">Chapter 12</a>)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<p class=\"semi-p\">In engineering practice, every <strong>3D stacking technology</strong> is also governed by two structural topology clauses—<strong>Bonding Orientation</strong> and <strong>Bonding Granularity</strong>:</p>\n<div class=\"table-container\"><table class=\"semi-table\"><thead><tr><th>3D Bonding Orientation &amp; Granularity Clause</th><th>Engineering Definition &amp; Interconnect Path</th><th>Trade-offs &amp; Representative Platforms</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Face-to-Face (F2F) Bonding</strong></td><td>The active top metal layers (BEOL faces) of the upper and lower dies are bonded directly against each other</td><td>Shortest possible signal path with zero TSV traversal between the paired dies; standard in two-tier <strong>TSMC SoIC-X (F2F)</strong>, <strong>Intel Foveros</strong>, and <strong>3D NAND CBA</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Face-to-Back (F2B) &amp; Back-to-Back (B2B) Bonding</strong></td><td>The front face of the upper die bonds to the thinned backside of the lower die, communicating through <strong>TSVs</strong> inside the lower die</td><td>Enables multi-story vertical scaling (3, 8, 12, or 16+ tiers); essential for <strong>HBM (8H/12H/16H)</strong>, <strong>3DS DRAM</strong>, and multi-tier <strong>SoIC / X-Cube</strong> stacks</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Wafer-to-Wafer (W2W / WoW) Bonding</strong></td><td>Two full 300 mm wafers are aligned and hybrid-bonded at once before dicing into 3D stacked cubes</td><td>Highest throughput and sub-200 nm alignment accuracy, but requires identical die sizes and cannot pre-screen bad dies; ideal for high-yield <strong>Sony Stacked CIS</strong> and <strong>3D NAND CBA</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Die-to-Wafer (D2W / CoW) &amp; Collective D2W Bonding</strong></td><td>Individual pre-tested <strong>Known Good Dies (KGD)</strong> are picked and bonded (individually or via collective carrier transfer) onto a target wafer or interposer</td><td>Allows mixing different die sizes and process nodes while avoiding compound yield loss from bad dies; standard for <strong>TSMC SoIC-X (CoW)</strong>, <strong>Intel Foveros Direct / Omni</strong>, and <strong>HBM</strong></td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<hr class=\"semi-hr\" />\n<h2 id=\"chiplets\" class=\"heading-anchor\">Chiplets<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#chiplets\" aria-hidden=\"true\">#</a></h2>\n<p class=\"semi-p\">Splitting a large chip into several smaller chips with independent functions and packaging them together is called a <strong>chiplet</strong> design. The industry is also promoting standard interfaces for connecting chips to each other, with the goal of letting chiplets from different sources be combined like building blocks.</p>\n<p class=\"semi-p\">As advanced packaging makes heavy use of lithography, electroplating, CMP and other processes that used to belong in the fab, the boundary between front-end manufacturing and back-end packaging is becoming more and more blurred.</p>\n<div class=\"table-container\"><table class=\"semi-table\"><thead><tr><th>Chiplet Interconnect Standard Clause</th><th>Target Packaging Tier (2D / 2.5D / 3D)</th><th>Key Specifications &amp; Ecosystem Role</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>UCIe (Universal Chiplet Interconnect Express)</strong><br>(<strong>UCIe-Standard</strong>, <strong>UCIe-Advanced</strong>, <strong>UCIe-3D</strong>)</td><td>• <strong>UCIe-Standard</strong>: Organic substrate (100–130 µm bumps)<br>• <strong>UCIe-Advanced</strong>: 2.5D CoWoS / EMIB (25–55 µm micro-bumps)<br>• <strong>UCIe-3D</strong>: 3D SoIC / Foveros Direct (&lt; 10 µm to sub-µm hybrid bonding)</td><td>Industry-wide open specification defining the physical layer (PHY), die-to-die adapter, and protocol mapping (PCIe, CXL, streaming) for plug-and-play multi-vendor chiplets</td></tr><tr><td><strong>AIB (Advanced Interface Bus)</strong> &amp; <strong>BoW (Bunch of Wires)</strong></td><td>2D organic substrates, 2.5D silicon bridges (EMIB), and interposers</td><td>Wide parallel clock-forwarded interfaces delivering low latency and high shoreline bandwidth density with minimal SerDes overhead</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Coherent High-Speed Fabric Links (NVLink-C2C / Infinity Fabric 2.5D &amp; 3D)</strong></td><td>2.5D CoWoS-S/L, 3D SoIC vertical stacks, and 3.5D hybrid packages</td><td>Cache-coherent, ultra-low-energy die-to-die fabrics tailored for tightly coupled CPU+GPU+SRAM AI supercomputing architectures</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"callout callout-knowhow\"><div class=\"callout-badge\">🔧 FAB KNOW-HOW</div><div class=\"callout-body\"><p class=\"semi-p\"><strong>🔧 Know-how | One bad chip can sink the whole package</strong></p>\n<ul class=\"semi-ul\"><li><strong>Situation</strong>: An advanced package contains eight chips.</li><li><strong>Practice</strong>: Every chip is fully tested before packaging to make sure it is a known good die (KGD), and the packaging process includes as many inspection points as possible.</li><li><strong>Why</strong>: Yields multiply. Even if every chip has 99% yield, the chance that all eight are good is only about 92%.</li><li><strong>If you skip it</strong>: If even one chip is bad, the whole expensive package, along with all the other good chips in it, is scrapped.</li><li><strong>Related chapters</strong>: <a href=\"#ch19\" class=\"semi-link\">Chapter 19: Wafer Test</a></li></ul>\n<p class=\"semi-p\"><strong>🔧 Know-how | Hybrid bonding needs front-end levels of cleanliness and flatness</strong></p>\n<ul class=\"semi-ul\"><li><strong>Situation</strong>: Two chips are to be bonded directly with hybrid bonding.</li><li><strong>Practice</strong>: The bonding surfaces go through extremely precise CMP, and the cleaning and environment before bonding must meet fab standards.</li><li><strong>Why</strong>: With no bumps to absorb anything between the two surfaces, a single particle props up a gap, and even slight unevenness causes poor bonding.</li><li><strong>If you skip it</strong>: One particle can cause a large number of surrounding contacts to fail at the same time.</li><li><strong>Related chapters</strong>: <a href=\"#ch08\" class=\"semi-link\">Chapter 8: CMP</a>, <a href=\"#ch09\" class=\"semi-link\">Chapter 9: Cleaning and Contamination Control</a></li></ul></div></div>\n<hr class=\"semi-hr\" />\n<h2 id=\"challenges-of-advanced-packaging\" class=\"heading-anchor\">Challenges of advanced packaging<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#challenges-of-advanced-packaging\" aria-hidden=\"true\">#</a></h2>\n<div class=\"table-container\"><table class=\"semi-table\"><thead><tr><th>Challenge</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Heat</td><td>With chips packed closely together or stacked, heat is harder to get out</td></tr><tr><td>Warpage</td><td>Different materials expand differently when heated, and the larger the package, the more it bends</td></tr><tr><td>Test</td><td>Once chips are stacked, the chips in the middle are hard to test individually</td></tr><tr><td>Multiplied yield</td><td>If any single chip or connection fails, the whole package is affected</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<hr class=\"semi-hr\" />\n<h2 id=\"known-25d-fan-out-and-3d-packaging-clauses\" class=\"heading-anchor\">2.5D, Fan-Out &amp; 3D/3.5D Packaging Clauses<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#known-25d-fan-out-and-3d-packaging-clauses\" aria-hidden=\"true\">#</a></h2>\n<div class=\"table-container\"><table class=\"semi-table\"><thead><tr><th>3D / 2.5D Engineering Challenge</th><th>Physical Bottleneck Mechanism</th><th>Industry Countermeasures &amp; Standard Clauses</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>3D Cross-Tier Thermal Resistance &amp; Hot-Spot Coupling</strong></td><td>Heat generated by bottom compute dies is trapped beneath stacked SRAM/DRAM tiers, while polymer underfill has much lower thermal conductivity than bulk silicon</td><td>Deploys <strong>structural dummy silicon</strong>, bumpless Cu-Cu hybrid bonding to eliminate gap resistance, <strong>indium / liquid-metal TIM1</strong>, direct-to-chip liquid cold plates, and microfluidic cooling channels</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Large-Area Warpage &amp; Chip-Package Interaction (CPI)</strong></td><td>CTE mismatch between silicon (~2.6 ppm/K), copper (~16.5 ppm/K), and organic ABF substrates (14–17 ppm/K) induces smiling/crying warpage and stresses fragile BEOL low-k dielectrics</td><td>Applies mechanical stiffener rings, MR-MUF encapsulation, CoWoS-R/L bridges, and next-gen <strong>TGV Glass Core Substrates</strong> with silicon-matched CTE</td></tr><tr><td><strong>3D Stack Test Access &amp; Lane Repair (3D DFT)</strong></td><td>Middle dies in a 3D stack cannot be physically probed once bonded</td><td>Mandates the <strong>IEEE 1838 3D DfT Standard</strong> (Primary/Secondary TAPs and Flexible Parallel Port [FPP]) combined with Wafer-Level Burn-In and <strong>built-in redundant TSV/bump lane repair</strong> in UCIe and HBM</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<hr class=\"semi-hr\" />\n<h2 id=\"quantitative-governing-laws-and-3d-process-windows\" class=\"heading-anchor\">Quantitative Governing Laws & 3D Process Windows<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#quantitative-governing-laws-and-3d-process-windows\" aria-hidden=\"true\">#</a></h2>\n<p class=\"semi-p\">Across 2.5D (CoWoS / EMIB), Fan-Out (InFO / FOPLP), and <strong>3D/3.5D bumpless hybrid bonding (SoIC / Foveros Direct / HBM / TGV Glass Substrates)</strong>, three quantitative physical scaling laws govern heterogeneous integration:</p>\n<div class=\"table-container\"><table class=\"semi-table\"><thead><tr><th>2.5D/3D Heterogeneous Integration Law</th><th>Governing Mathematical Formula</th><th>Cross-Generation Physical Benchmarks</th><th>Impact on AI Superchips, CPO &amp; TGV Glass Substrates</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td><strong>Inverse-Square Pitch Density ($1/P^2$) &amp; Energy-per-Bit Law</strong></td><td>$D_{\\text{IO}} = \\frac{1}{P_{\\text{pitch}}^2},\\quad E_{\\text{bit}} = \\frac{1}{2} C_{\\text{io}} V_{\\text{swing}}^2$</td><td>Scales from C4 Flip-Chip ($150\\ \\mu\\text{m} \\to 44\\text{ IO/mm}^2$, $\\sim 5\\text{ pJ/bit}$) $\\rightarrow$ 2.5D micro-bumps ($36\\ \\mu\\text{m} \\to 770\\text{ IO/mm}^2$, $\\sim 0.5\\text{ pJ/bit}$) $\\rightarrow$ <strong>3D Hybrid Bonding ($3\\ \\mu\\text{m} \\to 1.1\\times 10^5\\text{ IO/mm}^2$, $&lt; 0.05\\text{ pJ/bit}$)</strong></td><td>A $10\\times$ pitch reduction yields a $100\\times$ I/O density leap and $&gt;10\\times$ lower capacitance, making 3D stacked chiplets behave like a single monolithic die</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>3D Stacked IC Thermal Coupling Resistance Matrix Law</strong></td><td>$T_{j,k} = T_{\\text{coolant}} + \\sum_{m=1}^{N} R_{\\text{th},km}\\,P_m,\\quad \\Delta T_{\\text{3D}} \\propto \\sum_{k=1}^{N} P_k \\left(\\sum_{i=k}^{N} \\frac{t_i}{\\kappa_i A}\\right)$</td><td>In an $N$-tier stack (e.g., Logic-on-Memory or 16-Hi HBM4), heat from lower tiers must traverse upper dies and bond interfaces to reach the top cold plate</td><td>Drives placing high-power logic closest to the top heatsink and replacing polymer underfills with direct <code>Cu-Cu / SiO₂ hybrid bonding</code> and direct liquid cooling</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>Stoney Bimaterial Warpage &amp; Large-Package Scaling Law</strong></td><td>$\\kappa_{\\text{warp}} = \\frac{1}{R} = \\frac{6 E_f t_f (\\alpha_f - \\alpha_s)\\Delta T}{(1-\\nu_s) E_s t_s^2},\\quad w_{\\text{max}} \\approx \\frac{L_{\\text{pkg}}^2}{8 R}$</td><td>Maximum bow $w_{\\text{max}}$ grows quadratically with package body size $L_{\\text{pkg}}^2$ and inversely with substrate Young's modulus $E_s$</td><td>As AI packages exceed $100\\times 100\\text{ mm}^2$ (8–12× reticle size), organic warpage drives the transition to ultra-stiff, CTE-tailorable <strong>Through-Glass Via (TGV) Glass Core Substrates</strong></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<hr class=\"semi-hr\" />\n<h2 id=\"failure-signatures-and-root-cause-diagnostics\" class=\"heading-anchor\">Fab Failure Signatures & Root-Cause Diagnostics<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#failure-signatures-and-root-cause-diagnostics\" aria-hidden=\"true\">#</a></h2>\n<p class=\"semi-p\">2.5D/3D advanced packaging scales module areas to multi-reticle dimensions and stacks hundred-watt heat sources vertically: <strong>CoWoS room-to-reflow Smile/Cry warpage, 3D SoIC hybrid-bond particle voids, and 3D vertical thermal cross-heating</strong> are its three critical failure modes:</p>\n<div class=\"table-container\"><table class=\"semi-table\"><thead><tr><th>Fab Failure Signature &amp; Wafer/Electrical Symptom</th><th>Underlying Physical &amp; Process Root Cause</th><th>Cross-Station Metrology &amp; FA Verification</th><th>OCAP Containment &amp; Permanent Poka-Yoke</th></tr></thead><tbody>\n<tr><td><strong>Multi-Reticle CoWoS Smile-to-Cry Warpage Inversion (Non-Wet Open &amp; Center Bridging)</strong></td><td>Across $>2500\\text{ mm}^2$ packages, CTE mismatch bends the assembly into a convex \"Cry\" shape at $25^\\circ\\text{C}$ and inverts into a concave \"Smile\" at $250^\\circ\\text{C}$ reflow; warpage $>120\\text{ }\\mu\\text{m}$ crushes center bumps into shorts while lifting corner bumps into <strong>Non-Wet Opens (NWO) / Head-in-Pillow (HiP)</strong></td><td>Profile full-temperature-cycle 3D warpage ($25^\\circ\\text{C} \\leftrightarrow 260^\\circ\\text{C}$) via <strong>Shadow Moiré interferometry</strong> and inspect joints via 3D X-Ray CT</td><td>Attach a <strong>perimeter Cu/stainless-steel Stiffener Ring</strong>, tune molding compound $T_g$ and filler loading, and transition ultra-large packages to <strong>low-CTE Glass Core Substrates</strong></td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>Millimeter-Scale Hybrid-Bonding Blister Voids from a Single 50nm Particle</strong></td><td>Because silicon wafers have high flexural rigidity ($E \\approx 169\\text{ GPa}$), a single $50\\text{ nm}$ particle trapped at the $\\text{SiO}_2\\text{–SiO}_2$ interface props open a circular unbonded blister void $0.5\\text{–}2\\text{ mm}$ wide, disconnecting thousands of sub-micron Cu pads</td><td>Scan 100% of pre-bonded wafer/die pairs using <strong>Through-Silicon IR interferometry (Newton rings) and high-frequency C-SAM</strong> before $350^\\circ\\text{C}$ Cu-anneal lock-in</td><td>Operate hybrid bonders inside <strong>ISO Class 1 mini-environments</strong> with integrated <strong>in-situ megasonic $\\text{DIO}_3$ scrub + $\\text{N}_2/\\text{O}_2$ plasma activation</strong> seconds before contact</td></tr>\n<tr><td><strong>3D Vertical Thermal Cross-Heating &amp; Thermal Interface Material (TIM) Pump-Out</strong></td><td>Heat generated by a bottom logic die ($>1.5\\text{ W/mm}^2$) must traverse stacked bonding layers to reach the top heat spreader, baking stacked 3D SRAM or adjacent HBM cubes beyond their $85\\text{–}95^\\circ\\text{C}$ retention limit</td><td>Correlate per-tier on-die Digital Thermal Sensor (DTS) telemetry under burst workloads with C-SAM scans of the lid-to-die TIM interface after thermal cycling</td><td>Insert <strong>Structural Thermal Dummy Silicon + Thermal TSV arrays</strong>, Thin down top dies to minimize $R_{\\text{th}}$, and bond lids with <strong>soldered Indium metallic TIMs or direct-to-chip microchannel liquid cold plates</strong></td></tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<hr class=\"semi-hr\" />\n<h2 id=\"key-takeaways\" class=\"heading-anchor\">Key takeaways<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#key-takeaways\" aria-hidden=\"true\">#</a></h2>\n<ol class=\"semi-ol\"><li>Scaling keeps getting harder, and advanced packaging has become a new way to improve performance.</li><li>2.5D packaging places several chips side by side on an interposer, often a processor plus HBM.</li><li>Fan-out packaging uses redistribution layers to spread contacts outward and suits thin, light products.</li><li>3D stacking is moving from micro bumps to hybrid bonding, with ever-higher connection density.</li><li>Yields multiply, so every chip must be a known good die.</li></ol>\n<hr class=\"semi-hr\" />\n<h2 id=\"further-reading\" class=\"heading-anchor\">Further reading<a class=\"anchor-link\" href=\"#further-reading\" aria-hidden=\"true\">#</a></h2>\n<ul class=\"semi-ul\"><li>John H. Lau, <em>Semiconductor Advanced Packaging</em></li><li>Papers from IEEE ECTC (Electronic Components and Technology Conference)</li></ul>\n<hr class=\"semi-hr\" />\n<p class=\"semi-p\"><a href=\"#ch20\" class=\"semi-link\">← Chapter 20: Packaging</a> | <a href=\"#explore\" class=\"semi-link\">Contents</a> | <a href=\"#ch22\" class=\"semi-link\">Chapter 22: Final Test and Reliability →</a></p>"};
